Hi Mark,

The following code will do it:

PROC startwrd:
    LOCAL pName$(40),cmdl$(128),pid%
    pName$="ROM::WORD.APP"+CHR$(0)
    cmdl$="OWord"+CHR$(0)+".WRD"+CHR$(0)+"????????.???"+CHR$(0)
    IF CALL($0187,ADDR(pName$)+1,ADDR(cmdl$),0,0,ADDR(pid%))>=0
        CALL($0688,pid%)
    ENDIF
ENDP

The string "????????.???" should contain the path+filename of the file which
shall be initially loaded by the WORD-application.

Heinrich Hiemesch
reply to heinrich_hiemesch@m2.maus.de
not more than 64kB/d - thanks


Mark wrote:
MM>The subject says it - I would like to be able to start up either Word,
